{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Break off the golden rings.</b> Aaron intended it for the sake of Heaven. He reasoned in his heart: if I appoint one of the great men over them, tomorrow when Moses comes he will not wish to step down from his greatness, and quarrel and bloodshed will multiply among them; and if I do not appoint one for them, they will appoint him themselves, and the dispute will grow; and if I say I will be their head, the matter will be displeasing in Moses' eyes. I will keep them occupied until Moses comes, and I will do a thing that has no substance, and when Moses comes it will be annulled on its own — and so he did. Therefore he said, <b>break off the golden rings that are in the ears of your wives</b> etc., as Rashi explained."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:25.492012985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}